次こんな問題！

B.1. Get the output of the following OCaml code using this link or by asking an LLM to reason through it.

let dec r = r := !r - 1;;

let () =
  let x = ref 5 in
  while !x > 0 do
    Printf.printf "Hello\n";
    dec x;
  done;
;;


Haskell is considered to be a pure functional programming language. Is OCaml also a pure functional programming language? Explain why or why not by referencing the output of the above code snippet.


B.2. If we had to guess, the extent of what you’ve heard about OCaml is: (1) you have to use it in Eggert’s offering of CS131 and (2) JaneStreet uses OCaml. Do a little bit of research about the programming language OCaml and also about the company JaneStreet (an LLM is probably your friend here). Why do you think JaneStreet opted to use OCaml over Haskell?

昔Ocaml習ったと思うんだけど忘れた。
一問目から解いていきたいです！
